  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Opponent's only creature (Gifted Aetherborn) is summoning sick and cannot block. Opponent's lands are tapped. Attacking with Eternal Taskmaster deals 2 free damage with zero risk.",
      "actionTaken": "Declined to attack with Eternal Taskmaster.",
      "betterLine": "Attack with Eternal Taskmaster for 2 unblockable damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 44,
      "player": "GptOSS Snark",
      "decisionIndex": 18
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gifted Aetherborn (2/3 deathtouch lifelink) should attack here. The only untapped blocker is Pestermite (2/1) and the opponent has zero untapped mana for tricks. If Pestermite blocks, Aetherborn kills it with deathtouch, gains 2 life from lifelink, and survives. If unblocked, deals 2 and gains 2. Both outcomes are pure upside. Additionally, the lifelink could help enable Sanguine Indulgence's cost reduction later.",
      "actionTaken": "Declined to attack with Gifted Aetherborn",
      "betterLine": "Attack with Gifted Aetherborn. Either it gets through for 2 damage + 2 life, or it kills Pestermite in combat while surviving and gaining life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 87,
      "player": "GLM47 Philo",
      "decisionIndex": 28
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Last Gasp on Eternal Taskmaster (2/3) when they could have played Swamp first and cast Agonizing Syphon instead, which also kills the Taskmaster (3 damage to a 2/3) while gaining 3 life. At 14 life facing flyers, the 3 life is meaningful, and Last Gasp is preserved for a future threat that Agonizing Syphon couldn't handle (e.g., a 4+ toughness creature that needs -3/-3).",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Last Gasp targeting Eternal Taskmaster without playing land first",
      "betterLine": "Play Swamp first, then cast Agonizing Syphon targeting Eternal Taskmaster to kill it AND gain 3 life, preserving Last Gasp for future use",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 119,
      "player": "GLM47 Philo",
      "decisionIndex": 38
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chose 'Bird' for Instruments of War creature type, which doesn't match any creature currently on the battlefield (Pestermite is Faerie Rogue, Sentinels of Glen Elendra is Faerie Soldier), in hand (Dutiful Attendant is Human Warrior), or in graveyard (Eternal Taskmaster is Zombie). 'Faerie' wasn't available, but 'Horror' would have matched Gloom Sower if it's in the deck, providing potential future value.",
      "actionTaken": "Chose 'Bird' as the creature type for Instruments of War",
      "betterLine": "Choose 'Horror' to potentially buff Gloom Sower if drawn later, or another type with more relevance to likely future creatures in the deck",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 144,
      "player": "GptOSS Snark",
      "decisionIndex": 42
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Agonizing Syphon before playing the Swamp from hand. With the land played first (6 lands total), after spending 4 mana on Syphon, they'd have 2 Swamps untapped — enough to also cast Gifted Aetherborn (BB), a crucial 2/3 deathtouch lifelink creature at 10 life. Without the land, only 1 mana remains after Syphon, making the Aetherborn uncastable this turn.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Agonizing Syphon targeting Pestermite without first playing the Swamp from hand",
      "betterLine": "Play Swamp first, then cast Agonizing Syphon (4 mana), then cast Gifted Aetherborn with the remaining 2 black mana, deploying both a removal spell and a strong blocker in the same turn",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 158,
      "player": "GLM47 Philo",
      "decisionIndex": 45
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The opponent has zero available blockers (Sentinels of Glen Elendra is tapped, Dutiful Attendant has summoning sickness). Gifted Aetherborn could attack completely unblocked for 2 damage plus 2 lifelink, but was held back for no reason.",
      "actionTaken": "Attacked with only Ronom Unicorn for 2 damage, leaving Gifted Aetherborn back.",
      "betterLine": "Attack with both Ronom Unicorn and Gifted Aetherborn for 4 total damage and 2 life gained from lifelink, since the opponent has no available blockers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 205,
      "player": "GLM47 Philo",
      "decisionIndex": 53
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to equip Malefic Scythe (1 soul counter, giving +1/+1) to Sentinels of Glen Elendra before combat. The Sentinels has flying and can attack unblocked (opponent has no flyers). This would deal 3 damage instead of 2 to an opponent at 11 life, with no downside since GptOSS Snark has the mana available (1 of 3 untapped lands).",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority without equipping Malefic Scythe",
      "betterLine": "Equip Malefic Scythe to Sentinels of Glen Elendra for {1}, then attack with a 3/4 flyer for 3 unblockable damage instead of 2",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 239,
      "player": "GptOSS Snark",
      "decisionIndex": 61
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "GptOSS Snark is at 4 life facing a Gloom Sower (8/6) and Gifted Aetherborn (2/3 with deathtouch/lifelink) on the opponent's side. The opponent is at 11 life. Vendilion Clique is a 3/1 flash flyer that could be cast at instant speed later (e.g., on opponent's draw step or end step), but passing priority in the precombat main phase without casting it or equipping Malefic Scythe to a creature is a significant missed opportunity. With Malefic Scythe having 1 soul counter (+1/+1), equipping it to Eternal Taskmaster (making it 3/4) or Sentinels of Glen Elendra would improve board presence. More importantly, at 4 life with the opponent having an 8/6 and a 2/3 lifelinker, the player needs to maximize every resource. While Vendilion Clique has flash and could be cast later, passing the entire main phase without even equipping the Scythe (which costs {1} and is sorcery speed) wastes the equip opportunity entirely for this turn.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority in precombat main phase without casting Vendilion Clique or equipping Malefic Scythe.",
      "betterLine": "Equip Malefic Scythe to Sentinels of Glen Elendra (making it 4/5 flying) to have a stronger blocker against the Gloom Sower, then hold up Vendilion Clique for flash deployment. The equipped Sentinels could block the 8/6 Gloom Sower without dying, which is critical at 4 life. Alternatively, equip to Eternal Taskmaster to make it a 3/4 for better blocking options.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 275,
      "player": "GptOSS Snark",
      "decisionIndex": 67
    }
